
Things to do:

The Idea:
My idea is to build a offline study and focus tracker. It follows the design of a Tamagotchi with a modern revamp which is more minimalistic.
It should be able to track a study or focus session through a normal timer, stopwatch and pomodoro, along with a menu showing all your statistics and your study streaks.
It has simple animations of a character when you are in a study session or start or end it. Almost like a figure that grows or upgrades when you study more.
Maybe has different animations showing that its bored or focussed or some way to indicate low battery aswell. 
This all goes along with the fact that this will be small and portable, disconnected from the Internet to reduce distractions, chargeable by Type-C, 
and has a basic speaker in build giving sound effects when you start or end a session and when the battery is low. The figure, animations and sound effects will all be based on retro game style.
I want to build this because I feel that this could be useful for me given the fact that I am a high school student, and it can also help the community, including people who have trouble studying or focussing(part of this population).
This idea is inspired based on some of the projects I am working on for my school submissions and also PewDiePie's recent videos related to hardware building and self-hosting.

Websites to look at for parts:


Steps:
Find a display/screen that will be used
Create basic shape, and design with the dimensions of the thing
Look for the correct processor(raspberry Pi)
Look for the other parts that I will need like type C port, small speaker and any other auxiliary parts
Understand how will I code this and the softwares I need, get a basic understanding of them
Understand what in the world is a PCB and whether I need one, then create it
Make the designs with simple animations of the character and the sound effects
Start coding the thing
After software is ready and PCB is ready then 3D design a proper shell for the thing along with the buttons and speaker grill and type c port hole
Documentation and complete all the deliverables to submit the project.


